{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given number is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True if non-prime, False if prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True\n    if number == 2:\n        return False\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return True\n\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True\n        i += 2\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer n is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True if n is non-prime, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False  # Numbers less than 2 are neither prime nor non-prime\n    \n    # Iterate from 2 up to the square root of n (inclusive)\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True  # Found a divisor, so it's non-prime\n    \n    return False  # No divisors found, so it's prime\n```"}
