{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the minimum positive number of rotations required to transform a string back into its original form.\n    It iterates through possible rotation counts to find the smallest 'k' that restores the original string.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        rotated_s = s[k:] + s[:k]\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return k\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum positive number of rotations to return a string to its original form.\n    It assumes the input string is non-empty based on the critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    temp = s + s\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if temp[i:i + n] == s:\n            return i\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(text, char_to_remove):\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from the string.\n    If the character appears only once, only that single occurrence is removed.\"\"\"\n    first_idx = text.find(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return text\n\n    temp_text = text[:first_idx] + text[first_idx+1:]\n\n    last_idx = text.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if last_idx == first_idx:\n        return temp_text\n    else:\n        # Adjust the last index based on whether the first removal affected its position.\n        adjusted_last_idx = last_idx - 1 if last_idx > first_idx else last_idx\n        return temp_text[:adjusted_last_idx] + temp_text[adjusted_last_idx+1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string, char_to_remove):\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from the input string.\"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    # Remove first occurrence\n    temp_string = input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n\n    last_idx = temp_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n    if last_idx == -1:\n        return temp_string # Only one occurrence was found and removed\n\n    # Remove last occurrence from the temp_string\n    final_string = temp_string[:last_idx] + temp_string[last_idx + 1:]\n    return final_string"}
