{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "```python\ndef is_woodall(num):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for a non-negative integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    MAX_N_FOR_CHECK = 30  # Limits the search for 'n' to prevent excessive computation.\n\n    # Iterate through possible values of n, starting from 1 as Woodall numbers are generally positive.\n    for n in range(1, MAX_N_FOR_CHECK + 1):\n        woodall_candidate = n * (2**n) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == num:\n            return True\n        if woodall_candidate > num:\n            # If the current candidate is larger than 'num', all subsequent candidates will also be larger.\n            return False\n    return False\n```"}
