{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements within pairs in the given tuple list.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple_list: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains exactly two numeric values (int or float).\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum absolute difference found. Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list.\n        InvalidInputError: If any element in the list is not a tuple,\n                           if a tuple does not contain exactly two elements,\n                           or if elements within a tuple are not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(tuple_list):\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a tuple.\")\n        if len(item) != 2:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Tuple at index {i} does not contain exactly two elements.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in item):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {i} must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    differences = [abs(t[0] - t[1]) for t in tuple_list]\n    return max(differences)\n```"}
