{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(words: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a sequence of words adheres to a given pattern, ensuring a one-to-one mapping.\n    Returns True if the structural pattern is consistent across both lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(words) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    def _perform_mapping_check(list1: list[str], list2: list[str]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper to check for consistent one-way mapping from list1 to list2.\"\"\"\n        mapping = {}\n        for i in range(len(list1)):\n            char1 = list1[i]\n            char2 = list2[i]\n            if char1 in mapping:\n                if mapping[char1] != char2:\n                    return False  # Inconsistent mapping\n            else:\n                mapping[char1] = char2\n        return True\n\n    # Check mapping from words to patterns\n    if not _perform_mapping_check(words, patterns):\n        return False\n\n    # Check mapping from patterns to words to ensure one-to-one bidirectional mapping\n    if not _perform_mapping_check(patterns, words):\n        return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/72", "solution": "```python\ndef dif_Square(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number can be represented as the difference of two squares.\n    A number n can be represented as a^2 - b^2 if and only if n is odd or n is a multiple of 4.\n    Numbers of the form 4k + 2 cannot be represented.\n\n    Args:\n        num: The integer to check.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the number can be represented as the difference of two squares, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If num is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If num is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'num' must be an integer.\")\n    if num < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'num' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    return num % 2 == 1 or num % 4 == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(arr: list, patterns: list) -> bool:\n    if len(arr) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    arr_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_arr_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        arr_val = arr[i]\n        pattern_val = patterns[i]\n\n        if arr_val in arr_to_pattern_map:\n            if arr_to_pattern_map[arr_val] != pattern_val:\n                return False\n        else:\n            arr_to_pattern_map[arr_val] = pattern_val\n\n        if pattern_val in pattern_to_arr_map:\n            if pattern_to_arr_map[pattern_val] != arr_val:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_arr_map[pattern_val] = arr_val\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef find_tuples(list_of_tuples: List[Tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning only those where all elements are divisible by k.\n    This function expects integer elements in tuples and a non-zero integer k.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_tuples = []\n    for tup in list_of_tuples:\n        is_current_tuple_divisible = True\n        for element in tup:\n            if element % k != 0:\n                is_current_tuple_divisible = False\n                break\n        \n        if is_current_tuple_divisible:\n            filtered_tuples.append(tup)\n            \n    return filtered_tuples\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\ndef find_tuples(data_list, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning only those where all elements are divisible by k.\n    Empty tuples are excluded from the results.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_tuples = []\n\n    for current_tuple in data_list:\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        \n        # As per design, empty tuples are not considered to have all elements divisible.\n        if not current_tuple:\n            all_elements_divisible = False\n        else:\n            for element in current_tuple:\n                # Trusting caller inputs: element is int, k is non-zero int.\n                if element % k != 0:\n                    all_elements_divisible = False\n                    break\n\n        # Add the tuple if all its (non-empty) elements are divisible.\n        if all_elements_divisible and current_tuple:\n            filtered_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n            \n    return filtered_tuples\n```"}
