{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "_memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1))\n    p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n    term1 = sequence(p_n_minus_1)\n    term2 = sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n    result = term1 + term2\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth term of the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    The sequence is defined as:\n    P(1) = 1\n    P(2) = 1\n    P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2\n\n    Args:\n        n: The positive integer position in the sequence (n > 0).\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth Newman-Conway number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    _memo = {1: 1, 2: 1} # Initialize memoization cache for this specific function call\n\n    def _calculate(k):\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n\n        # P(k) = P(P(k-1)) + P(k-P(k-1))\n        # The recursive calls here must refer to the inner _calculate function\n        term_k_minus_1 = _calculate(k - 1)\n        term_p_k_minus_1 = _calculate(term_k_minus_1)\n        term_k_minus_p_k_minus_1 = _calculate(k - term_k_minus_1)\n\n        _memo[k] = term_p_k_minus_1 + term_k_minus_p_k_minus_1\n        return _memo[k]\n\n    return _calculate(n)\n```"}
