{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "```python\ndef is_undulating(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number's digits strictly alternate (e.g., 12121 or 545).\n    Single-digit numbers are considered undulating.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(abs(number))\n\n    if len(num_str) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate from the third digit to check the alternating pattern.\n    for i in range(2, len(num_str)):\n        if num_str[i] != num_str[i-2] or num_str[i] == num_str[i-1]:\n            return False\n    \n    # For two-digit numbers, they are undulating only if their digits are different.\n    if len(num_str) == 2:\n        return num_str[0] != num_str[1]\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "```python\ndef is_undulating(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the digits of the input number follow an alternating pattern.\n    Applies the check to the absolute value of the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_number = str(abs(number))\n    n = len(s_number)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n    if n == 2:\n        return s_number[0] != s_number[1]\n\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if s_number[i] != s_number[i-2]:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
