{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "```python\ndef index_minimum(data: list[tuple]) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first element of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    Assumes `data` is a non-empty list of tuples, each with at least two comparable elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_value = data[0][1]\n    result_first_value = data[0][0]\n\n    for item in data[1:]:\n        current_second_value = item[1]\n        if current_second_value < min_value:\n            min_value = current_second_value\n            result_first_value = item[0]\n\n    return result_first_value\n```"}
