{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of positive divisors for a given integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of n to find divisors.\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            # If i divides n, then n/i also divides n.\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1  # Count only once for perfect squares.\n            else:\n                count += 2  # Count i and n/i.\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef divisor(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of divisors for a given positive integer.\n    The function iterates up to the square root of the number for efficient computation.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    sqrt_n = int(math.sqrt(number))\n\n    for i in range(1, sqrt_n + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            if i * i == number:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n\n    return count\n```"}
