{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(decimal_num: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a non-negative decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n    Assumes valid, non-negative integer input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_num == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    current_num = decimal_num\n    while current_num > 0:\n        binary_digits.append(str(current_num % 2))\n        current_num //= 2\n\n    return \"\".join(reversed(binary_digits))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(decimal_num: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a non-negative integer decimal number to its binary equivalent,\n    represented as a string with no leading zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_num == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    binary_string = \"\"\n    temp_num = decimal_num\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        remainder = temp_num % 2\n        binary_string = str(remainder) + binary_string\n        temp_num //= 2\n    return binary_string\n```"}
