{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts odd decimal numbers from binary string rotations.\n    Performs left circular rotations and converts to decimal.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(num_rotations):\n        decimal_value = int(current_binary_string, 2)\n        \n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        current_binary_string = current_binary_string[1:] + current_binary_string[0]\n    \n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(s: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total count of times an odd integer was encountered\n    during n left rotations of the binary string s.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_s = s\n    \n    # Iterate n times, processing the initial string as the 0th rotation\n    for _ in range(n):\n        # Convert the current binary string to its decimal integer equivalent\n        decimal_int = int(current_s, 2)\n        \n        # Determine if the decimal integer is odd\n        if decimal_int % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n        # Rotate the string one position to the left for the next iteration\n        if current_s: # Ensure string is not empty before rotating\n            current_s = current_s[1:] + current_s[0]\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any, Set\n\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all inner lists within a given list of lists.\n    Returns a list of common elements; returns empty if no common elements or input is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return []\n\n    # Start with the set of elements from the first list.\n    common_elements: Set[Any] = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Intersect with subsequent lists, stopping early if no common elements remain.\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(set(nested_lists[i]))\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return list(common_elements)\n```"}
