{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "```python\ndef _sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a positive integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n            \n    total_sum = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n            if i * i != n:\n                total_sum += n // i\n    return total_sum\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sums all amicable numbers up to a specified limit n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    amicable_numbers_found = set()\n    for num in range(1, n + 1):\n        if num in amicable_numbers_found:\n            continue\n\n        sum_divisors_num = _sum_proper_divisors(num)\n        \n        if sum_divisors_num > num and sum_divisors_num <= n:\n            sum_divisors_m = _sum_proper_divisors(sum_divisors_num)\n            if sum_divisors_m == num:\n                amicable_numbers_found.add(num)\n                amicable_numbers_found.add(sum_divisors_num)\n    \n    return sum(amicable_numbers_found)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "```python\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to a specified limit.\n    It uses a nested helper function and an in-memory cache for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(n: int) -> int:\n        # Calculates the sum of all positive divisors of n excluding n itself.\n        # Iterates up to the square root of n to find divisors efficiently.\n        if n == 1:\n            return 0\n        s = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                s += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    s += n // i\n        return s\n\n    # This dictionary acts as the AmicableDivisorCache, storing pre-calculated divisor sums.\n    # It uses direct dictionary operations as per the critical requirements.\n    divisor_cache: dict[int, int] = {}\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if i in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        # Retrieve sum_i from cache or calculate and store it.\n        sum_i = divisor_cache.get(i)\n        if sum_i is None:\n            sum_i = _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(i)\n            divisor_cache[i] = sum_i\n\n        # Check for potential amicable pairs with sum_i.\n        if sum_i > i and sum_i <= limit:\n            # Retrieve sum_j from cache or calculate and store it.\n            sum_j = divisor_cache.get(sum_i)\n            if sum_j is None:\n                sum_j = _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(sum_i)\n                divisor_cache[sum_i] = sum_j\n            \n            # If sum_j equals i, then (i, sum_i) forms an amicable pair.\n            if sum_j == i:\n                total_sum += i + sum_i\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(i)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(sum_i)\n                \n    return total_sum\n```"}
