{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\nVOWELS = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses only the vowels in a given string.\n    'y' is not considered a vowel.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_list = list(s)\n    vowel_indices = [i for i, char in enumerate(s_list) if char.lower() in VOWELS]\n    \n    if not vowel_indices:\n        return s\n\n    vowels_only = [s_list[i] for i in vowel_indices]\n    reversed_vowels = vowels_only[::-1]\n\n    for i, original_index in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        s_list[original_index] = reversed_vowels[i]\n\n    return \"\".join(s_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the positions of only the vowels in the input string, preserving non-vowel positions.\n    Vowels are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u' (case-insensitive); 'y' is not a vowel.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    def is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given character is a vowel (case-insensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in VOWELS_SET\n\n    s_list = list(s)\n    left, right = 0, len(s_list) - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        while left < right and not is_vowel(s_list[left]):\n            left += 1\n        while left < right and not is_vowel(s_list[right]):\n            right -= 1\n\n        if left < right:\n            s_list[left], s_list[right] = s_list[right], s_list[left]\n            left += 1\n            right -= 1\n        \n    return \"\".join(s_list)\n```"}
