{"task_id": "Mbpp/140", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_singly(input_collection):\n    \"\"\"Flattens a nested list or tuple of numbers into a single set of unique integers and floats.\n    It recursively traverses the input, adding only numeric values to the result set.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_numbers = set()\n\n    def _flatten_recursive(current_item):\n        \"\"\"Recursively processes items, adding numbers to the outer set.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(current_item, (list, tuple)):\n            for item in current_item:\n                _flatten_recursive(item)\n        elif isinstance(current_item, (int, float)):\n            unique_numbers.add(current_item)\n\n    _flatten_recursive(input_collection)\n    return unique_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef _flip(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of elements from index 0 up to index k in-place.\"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    while start < k:\n        arr[start], arr[k] = arr[k], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        k -= 1\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements of the list arr.\"\"\"\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements using the Pancake Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list containing the elements of data in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(data)\n\n    arr = list(data)\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, current_size)\n\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            _flip(arr, current_size - 1)\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef _flip(arr, i):\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of elements in arr from index 0 up to (and including) index i.\"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    while start < i:\n        arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        i -= 1\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements of the list arr.\"\"\"\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements in-place using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    It returns the reference to the modified (sorted) input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, current_size)\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            _flip(arr, current_size - 1)\n    return arr\n```\n"}
