{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def gcd(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the greatest common divisor of two integers, returning gcd(|a|, |b|) as a non-negative result.\"\"\"\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n\ndef extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm.\n    Returns (g, x, y) such that ax + by = g, where g is gcd(a, b).\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return (b, 0, 1)\n    g, x1, y1 = extended_gcd(b % a, a)\n    x = y1 - (b // a) * x1\n    y = x1\n    return (g, x, y)\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n    \n    # extended_gcd returns (g_ext, x0, y0) such that a*x0 + b*y0 = g_ext.\n    # g_ext is gcd(a, b) but might be negative depending on a, b inputs.\n    g_ext, x0, y0 = extended_gcd(a, b)\n    \n    # A solution exists if and only if n is divisible by g_ext.\n    if n % g_ext != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Calculate the scaling factor using g_ext.\n    # This correctly handles cases where g_ext is negative.\n    scale_factor = n // g_ext\n    \n    x = x0 * scale_factor\n    y = y0 * scale_factor\n    \n    return (x, y)"}
