{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the smallest power of 2 that is greater than or equal to n.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # If n is already a power of 2, return n\n    if (n & (n - 1)) == 0:\n        return n\n\n    # Find the next power of 2 using bit manipulation\n    # Decrement n, then set all bits below the most significant bit to 1, then increment.\n    n -= 1\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    n |= n >> 32\n    return n + 1\n```"}
