{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if x is the majority element in the sorted array arr.\n    An element is a majority element if its count is strictly greater than n/2.\"\"\"\n\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], low: int, high: int, x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of x using binary search.\n        Returns the index or -1 if x is not found.\"\"\"\n        first = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                first = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:  # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first\n\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], low: int, high: int, x: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of x using binary search.\n        Returns the index or -1 if x is not found.\"\"\"\n        last = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                last = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:  # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last\n\n    # Input validation and error handling are excluded per critical requirements.\n    # The case n=0 is handled gracefully as _find_first_occurrence returns -1.\n\n    first_index = _find_first_occurrence(arr, 0, n - 1, x)\n\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_index = _find_last_occurrence(arr, 0, n - 1, x)\n    \n    count = last_index - first_index + 1\n    return count > n / 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is a majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    An element is a majority element if it occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _find_first(arr, n, x):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of x in arr using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, n - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def _find_last(arr, n, x):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of x in arr using binary search.\"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, n - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == x:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            elif arr[mid] < x:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > x\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    first_occurrence = _find_first(arr, n, x)\n    if first_occurrence == -1:\n        return False  # Element not found\n\n    last_occurrence = _find_last(arr, n, x)\n    \n    count = last_occurrence - first_occurrence + 1\n    return count > n / 2\n```"}
