{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits of a non-negative integer to 1.\n    Odd-indexed bits remain unchanged.\"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the highest bit position of the number.\n    # For number = 0, bit_length() is 0, making highest_bit -1.\n    highest_bit = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Generate a mask where all even-indexed bits are set to 1,\n    # up to the highest bit position of the input number.\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(0, highest_bit + 1, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set all relevant even bits.\n    return number | mask\n```"}
