{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "```python\ndef dog_age(age: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on human years.\n    It follows a specific conversion logic for the first two and subsequent years.\"\"\"\n\n    # First two human years: 10.5 dog years per human year.\n    # Subsequent human years (from the third year onwards): 4 dog years per human year.\n    if age <= 2:\n        return age * 10.5\n    else:\n        dog_years = 2 * 10.5  # Age for the first two human years\n        dog_years += (age - 2) * 4.0 # Age for subsequent human years\n        return dog_years\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "```python\ndef dog_age(human_years: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in \"dog years\" based on human years.\n    Applies rules: 10.5 dog years per human year for the first two, then 4 dog years per year thereafter.\"\"\"\n    if human_years <= 2:\n        dog_years = human_years * 10.5\n    else:\n        dog_years = (2 * 10.5) + ((human_years - 2) * 4)\n    return dog_years\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef list_split(input_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list into 'n' sublists, collecting elements at regular 'n'-th intervals.\n    Each sublist `i` contains elements from `input_list` at indices `i, i+n, i+2n, ...`.\n    \"\"\"\n    result: List[List[Any]] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for index, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result[index % n].append(item)\n    return result\n```"}
