{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i],\n    ensuring arr[k] is included and is the last element in its prefix segment.\n    \"\"\"\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Calculate max sum increasing subsequence ending at each index j within arr[0...i].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j]\n        for p in range(j):\n            if arr[j] > arr[p]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[p] + arr[j])\n\n    # Initialize with arr[k], in case no prefix elements can precede it.\n    max_subsequence_sum = arr[k]\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp that can be extended by arr[k].\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_subsequence_sum = max(max_subsequence_sum, dp[j] + arr[k])\n\n    return max_subsequence_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence within arr[0...i] that includes arr[k].\n    The subsequence must be strictly increasing and end with arr[k].\n    \"\"\"\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[current_idx] = arr[current_idx]\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if arr[current_idx] > arr[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + arr[current_idx])\n\n    max_sum = arr[k]\n\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[k] > arr[j]:\n            max_sum = max(max_sum, dp[j] + arr[k])\n        \n    return max_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef large_product(list1, list2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k largest products formed by selecting one factor from each list.\n    Returns an empty list if k is not positive or if either input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0 or not list1 or not list2:\n        return []\n\n    all_products = []\n    for num1 in list1:\n        for num2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(num1 * num2)\n\n    largest_k_products = heapq.nlargest(k, all_products)\n\n    return largest_k_products\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef large_product(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all possible products from two lists and returns the n largest.\n    Assumes valid list inputs and a positive integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list1 or not list2:\n        return []\n\n    all_products = [x * y for x, y in product(list1, list2)]\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return all_products[:n]\n```"}
