{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit (0) in an integer to 1.\n    If all bits are already set, the original number is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (number & (1 << i)):\n            return number | (1 << i)\n\n    return number\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in a non-negative integer. If all bits up to its most significant bit are set, it sets the next higher bit.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n\n    return n | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
