{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for a given non-negative integer n based on the recursive equation.\n    Uses memoization to store previously computed results.\"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        _memo[n] = n\n        return n\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2)\n        + get_max_sum(n // 3)\n        + get_max_sum(n // 4)\n        + get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n    \n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n using a recursive formula with memoization.\n    It adheres to f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n) using integer division.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Recursively compute sums of parts using integer division\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
