{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for all numbers in a given list.\n    Assumes inputs are a list of non-negative integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        # Calculate sum of digits for a single number\n        current_num_digit_sum = 0\n        num_str = str(number)\n        for digit_char in num_str:\n            current_num_digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n        total_sum += current_num_digit_sum\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits for each number in a given list,\n    and then returns the total sum of these individual digit sums.\n    Handles negative numbers by summing the digits of their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_all_digits = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        current_sum_of_digits = 0\n        abs_number = abs(number)\n\n        # Handle the special case for 0\n        if abs_number == 0:\n            current_sum_of_digits = 0\n        else:\n            # Calculate sum of digits for the current number\n            while abs_number > 0:\n                current_sum_of_digits += abs_number % 10\n                abs_number //= 10\n        total_sum_of_all_digits += current_sum_of_digits\n    return total_sum_of_all_digits\n```"}
