{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(numbers: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the pair of integers within a list that yields the highest product.\n    This function assumes the input list contains at least two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n    n = len(sorted_numbers)\n\n    # Compare the product of the two largest numbers with the product of the two smallest numbers.\n    prod1 = sorted_numbers[n-1] * sorted_numbers[n-2]\n    pair1 = (sorted_numbers[n-2], sorted_numbers[n-1])\n\n    prod2 = sorted_numbers[0] * sorted_numbers[1]\n    pair2 = (sorted_numbers[0], sorted_numbers[1])\n\n    if prod1 >= prod2:\n        return pair1\n    else:\n        return pair2\n```"}
