{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidSideLengthError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid trapezium side lengths.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef median_trapezium(side1: float, side2: float, side3: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median length of a trapezium from its two parallel sides.\n\n    Args:\n        side1: The length of the first parallel side.\n        side2: The length of the second parallel side.\n        side3: A third side length (ignored for median length calculation based on the standard definition).\n\n    Returns:\n        The calculated median length.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidSideLengthError: If side1, side2, or side3 are not positive numbers or are not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    for side, name in [(side1, \"side1\"), (side2, \"side2\"), (side3, \"side3\")]:\n        if not isinstance(side, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidSideLengthError(f\"{name} must be numeric.\")\n        if side <= 0:\n            raise InvalidSideLengthError(f\"{name} must be a positive number.\")\n\n    return (side1 + side2) / 2\n```"}
