{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\nADVERB_SUFFIX = \"ly\"\n\ndef _strip_trailing_punctuation(word: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes any non-alphanumeric characters from the end of the word.\n    Uses regex to substitute trailing non-word characters with an empty string.\"\"\"\n    return re.sub(r'[^\\\\w]*$', '', word)\n\ndef _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a cleaned word ends with the defined adverb suffix, case-insensitive.\n    Ensures the word is longer than just the suffix to prevent false positives.\"\"\"\n    return word.lower().endswith(ADVERB_SUFFIX) and len(word) > len(ADVERB_SUFFIX)\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first adverb in a sentence, returning its position and cleaned word.\n    Adverbs are identified by ending with 'ly' after stripping trailing punctuation.\"\"\"\n\n    # Regex to find word-like tokens and their spans, or isolated punctuation.\n    # It captures whole words (with internal hyphens/apostrophes) or non-word character sequences.\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\\\b\\\\w+[\\\\w\\\\\\'-]*\\\\b|[^\\\\s\\\\w]+', sentence):\n        word_text = match.group(0)\n        start_index = match.start()\n        end_index = match.end()\n\n        # Clean the word by stripping any trailing punctuation.\n        cleaned_word = _strip_trailing_punctuation(word_text)\n        \n        # Check if the cleaned word meets the adverb criteria.\n        if _is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            return (start_index, end_index, cleaned_word)\n    \n    # Return None if no adverb is found after processing the entire sentence.\n    return None\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\n\n# Predefined lists for adverb identification rules, based on the AdverbRules class.\n# These are kept in global scope to be \"defined in the same code block\" as the main function.\n_COMMON_ADVERBS_LOWER = {\n    \"always\", \"never\", \"often\", \"rarely\", \"sometimes\", \"usually\", \"very\",\n    \"quite\", \"rather\", \"too\", \"enough\", \"hardly\", \"scarcely\", \"just\",\n    \"almost\", \"already\", \"still\", \"yet\", \"soon\", \"today\", \"yesterday\",\n    \"tomorrow\", \"now\", \"then\", \"here\", \"there\", \"everywhere\", \"nowhere\",\n    \"somewhere\", \"anywhere\", \"up\", \"down\", \"in\", \"out\", \"away\", \"back\",\n    \"forward\", \"well\", \"fast\", \"late\", \"early\", \"daily\", \"weekly\", \"monthly\",\n    \"yearly\", \"much\", \"little\", \"more\", \"most\", \"less\", \"least\", \"also\",\n    \"even\", \"only\", \"else\", \"indeed\", \"perhaps\", \"maybe\", \"probably\",\n    \"certainly\", \"definitely\", \"obviously\", \"clearly\", \"actually\", \"really\"\n}\n_ADVERB_SUFFIXES_LOWER = {\"ly\", \"ward\", \"wards\", \"wise\"}\n\ndef _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a word is an adverb based on common adverbs or suffixes.\"\"\"\n    word_lower = word.lower()\n    if word_lower in _COMMON_ADVERBS_LOWER:\n        return True\n    for suffix in _ADVERB_SUFFIXES_LOWER:\n        if word_lower.endswith(suffix) and len(word_lower) > len(suffix):\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its positions in a given sentence.\n    It identifies adverbs using a predefined list or common suffixes.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Tokenize sentence into words and find their positions using regex.\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\b\\w+\\b', sentence):\n        word = match.group(0)\n        start_pos = match.start()\n        end_pos = match.end()\n\n        # Check if the extracted word is an adverb using the defined rules.\n        if _is_adverb(word):\n            return (start_pos, end_pos, word)\n\n    return None\n```"}
