{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\ndef index_multiplication(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise multiplication of two nested tuple structures.\n    It iterates through corresponding elements and returns their products.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_outer_list = []\n    for sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        result_inner_list = []\n        for element1, element2 in zip(sub_tuple1, sub_tuple2):\n            product = element1 * element2\n            result_inner_list.append(product)\n        result_outer_list.append(tuple(result_inner_list))\n\n    return tuple(result_outer_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(tuple1: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...], tuple2: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]) -> tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements from two input tuples of tuples.\n    Assumes inputs are valid and have matching dimensions and numerical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_outer_tuple = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        inner_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        inner_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        result_inner_tuple = []\n        for j in range(len(inner_tuple1)):\n            val1 = inner_tuple1[j]\n            val2 = inner_tuple2[j]\n            result_inner_tuple.append(val1 * val2)\n        result_outer_tuple.append(tuple(result_inner_tuple))\n\n    return tuple(result_outer_tuple)"}
