{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of pairs (a, b) from the input list `arr` such that `a ^ b` is odd.\n    This occurs when one integer is even and the other is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    count_even = 0\n    count_odd = 0\n\n    for x in arr:\n        if x % 2 == 0:\n            count_even += 1\n        else:\n            count_odd += 1\n\n    return count_even * count_odd\n```"}
