{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the absolute per-digit differences between two non-negative integers.\n    The shorter number is padded with leading zeros to match the length of the longer number.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_num1 = str(num1)\n    s_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(s_num1), len(s_num2))\n\n    s_num1 = s_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    s_num2 = s_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_diff = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(s_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(s_num2[i])\n        total_diff += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_diff\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n\n    The shorter number is conceptually padded with leading zeros to match\n    the length of the longer number for digit-wise comparison.\n\n    Args:\n        num1: The first non-negative integer.\n        num2: The second non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total sum of the per-digit differences.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(num1)\n    str_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n\n    # Pad the shorter number with leading zeros\n    padded_num1 = str_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_num2 = str_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_diff = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        total_diff += abs(int(padded_num1[i]) - int(padded_num2[i]))\n\n    return total_diff\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(nums: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist in the given list.\n    Implements Kadane's algorithm.\n    The 'length' parameter is included for signature compatibility but is not used in the algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(nums, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'nums' must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in nums):\n        raise ValueError(\"List 'nums' must contain only integers.\")\n    if not isinstance(length, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'length' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize max_so_far and current_max with the first element\n    # This handles the case where all numbers are negative correctly\n    max_so_far = nums[0]\n    current_max = nums[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        current_max = max(nums[i], current_max + nums[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum(nums: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist in the given list.\n    Implements Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = -math.inf\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for num in nums:\n        current_max += num\n        if current_max > max_so_far:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n    \n    if max_so_far == -math.inf:\n        return max(nums)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
