{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_values(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts all substrings enclosed in single or double quotation marks.\n    Handles escaped quotes within the quoted strings by unescaping them.\"\"\"\n    extracted_values = []\n    i = 0\n    n = len(text)\n    \n    while i < n:\n        current_char = text[i]\n        \n        if current_char == \"'\":\n            # Start of a single-quoted string\n            content_start_idx = i + 1\n            j = content_start_idx\n            \n            while j < n:\n                if text[j] == \"'\" and text[j-1] != '\\\\':\n                    # Found closing single quote, not escaped\n                    extracted_content = text[content_start_idx:j]\n                    extracted_values.append(extracted_content.replace(\"\\\\'\", \"'\"))\n                    i = j + 1 # Move past the closing quote\n                    break\n                j += 1\n            else:\n                # No closing quote found, implicitly skip this unclosed quote.\n                i += 1 \n        \n        elif current_char == '\"':\n            # Start of a double-quoted string\n            content_start_idx = i + 1\n            j = content_start_idx\n            \n            while j < n:\n                if text[j] == '\"' and text[j-1] != '\\\\':\n                    # Found closing double quote, not escaped\n                    extracted_content = text[content_start_idx:j]\n                    extracted_values.append(extracted_content.replace('\\\\\"', '\"'))\n                    i = j + 1 # Move past the closing quote\n                    break\n                j += 1\n            else:\n                # No closing quote found, implicitly skip this unclosed quote.\n                i += 1\n        else:\n            # Not a quote, move to the next character\n            i += 1\n            \n    return extracted_values\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Pairs(data_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unordered pairs of unequal elements within a list of integers.\n    This function manually tallies element occurrences and calculates pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    element_counts = {}\n    for item in data_list:\n        element_counts[item] = element_counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n    \n    unique_elements = list(element_counts.keys())\n\n    total_pairs = 0\n    # Calculate combinations of distinct unique elements by multiplying their counts.\n    for i in range(len(unique_elements)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_elements)):\n            elem1 = unique_elements[i]\n            elem2 = unique_elements[j]\n            total_pairs += element_counts[elem1] * element_counts[elem2]\n    \n    return total_pairs\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef count_Pairs(arr: List[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs with unequal elements in a list.\n    This function processes the list to find frequencies and then applies combinatorial logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequencies = {}\n    for x in arr:\n        frequencies[x] = frequencies.get(x, 0) + 1\n\n    total_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n\n    equal_pairs = 0\n    for count in frequencies.values():\n        if count >= 2:\n            equal_pairs += count * (count - 1) // 2\n\n    return total_pairs - equal_pairs\n```"}
