{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "```python\ndef two_unique_nums(numbers: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns numbers that appear exactly once in the input list,\n    preserving their original relative order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    unique_list = [num for num in numbers if counts[num] == 1]\n\n    return unique_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "```python\ndef two_unique_nums(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns numbers that appear exactly once in the input list.\n    The order of the unique numbers in the result list preserves their first appearance order.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    unique_list = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            unique_list.append(num)\n\n    return unique_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "```python\ndef unique_product(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of unique numbers in a given list.\n    Returns 1 if the list of unique numbers is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_elements = set(numbers)\n    product = 1\n    for num in unique_elements:\n        product *= num\n    return product\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "```python\ndef unique_product(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of unique numbers in a list.\n    Returns 1 for an empty list, following the multiplicative identity convention.\"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 1\n\n    unique_nums = set(numbers)\n    product = 1\n    for num in unique_nums:\n        product *= num\n    return product\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sub_Array(list1: list, list2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if `list2` is a contiguous sublist of `list1`.\n    Returns a boolean indicating the presence of `list2` in `list1`.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(list1)\n    m = len(list2)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if list1[i:i+m] == list2:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
