{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "```python\ndef last_Digit_Factorial(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given non-negative number.\n    Returns 0 for num >= 5, and 1 for 0!.\"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return 1\n    if num >= 5:\n        return 0\n\n    # Last digits for 1!, 2!, 3!, 4!\n    # 0! = 1 (handled above)\n    # 1! = 1\n    # 2! = 2\n    # 3! = 6\n    # 4! = 24 (last digit is 4)\n    factorials_last_digits = [1, 1, 2, 6, 4]\n    return factorials_last_digits[num]\n```"}
