{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "```python\ndef get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates Ludic numbers up to a given integer n using a sieve process.\n    The number 1 is always Ludic and subsequent numbers are sieved based on earlier Ludics.\n    \"\"\"\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n\n    while numbers:\n        k = numbers.pop(0)  # The current Ludic number is the first in the remaining list, then removed.\n        ludic_numbers.append(k)\n\n        if k == 1:\n            # The number 1 is Ludic but does not sieve out other numbers from the list.\n            continue\n\n        temp_numbers = []\n        # Remove every k-th element from the *remaining* 'numbers' list, based on their 1-indexed position.\n        for i in range(len(numbers)):\n            if (i + 1) % k != 0:\n                temp_numbers.append(numbers[i])\n        numbers = temp_numbers\n        \n    return ludic_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/604", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_words(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of words in a given string.\n    Words are delimited by one or more spaces, and the output uses single spaces.\"\"\"\n    words = input_string.split()\n    words.reverse()\n    return \" \".join(words)\n```"}
