{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bell_triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i-1][j-1] + bell_triangle[i][j-1]\n\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n    The Bell number B(n) is the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\"\"\"\n    # Initialize the Bell triangle, where bell_triangle[i][0] will store B(i)\n    bell_triangle = [[1]]\n\n    # Extend the Bell triangle up to n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row\n        row = [bell_triangle[i-1][-1]]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Subsequent elements are calculated using the sum of previous elements\n            next_val = row[j-1] + bell_triangle[i-1][j-1]\n            row.append(next_val)\n        bell_triangle.append(row)\n\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_kth_element(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the k-th element (1-indexed) from a list and returns a new list.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The original list.\n        k: The 1-indexed position of the element to remove.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list with the k-th element removed.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If input_list is not a list or k is not an integer.\n        IndexError: If k is out of bounds (1 <= k <= len(input_list)).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"k must be an integer\")\n\n    if not (1 <= k <= len(input_list)):\n        raise IndexError(f\"k ({k}) is out of bounds for list of length {len(input_list)}\")\n\n    # Convert 1-indexed k to 0-indexed\n    index_to_remove = k - 1\n    \n    # Create a new list by slicing and concatenating\n    return input_list[:index_to_remove] + input_list[index_to_remove + 1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_kth_element(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list with the k-th element removed from input_list, without modifying the original.\n    Handles empty lists and out-of-bounds k gracefully by returning a copy of the original (or empty) list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    if not (0 <= k < len(input_list)):\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    new_list = input_list[:k] + input_list[k+1:]\n    return new_list\n```"}
