{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "```python\ndef max_of_nth(matrix: list[list[int | float]], n: int) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Returns the maximum value of the n-th column in a given matrix.\n    The matrix is a list of lists, and n is the zero-based column index.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_rows = len(matrix)\n\n    # Initialize max_val with the first element of the specified column.\n    # Trusting the caller's inputs, matrix is non-empty and n is a valid index.\n    max_val = matrix[0][n]\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the rows to find the maximum in the n-th column.\n    for i in range(1, num_rows):\n        if matrix[i][n] > max_val:\n            max_val = matrix[i][n]\n            \n    return max_val\n```"}
