{"task_id": "Mbpp/614", "solution": "```python\ndef cummulative_sum(data: list[tuple[int, ...]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the cumulative sum of all integer values present in a given list of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains zero or more integer values.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total cumulative sum of all integers.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input 'data' is not a list or contains non-tuple elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for item_tuple in data:\n        if not isinstance(item_tuple, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'data' must be tuples, but found: {type(item_tuple)}\")\n        for value in item_tuple:\n            if isinstance(value, int):\n                total_sum += value\n    return total_sum\n```"}
