{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise modulo operation on two tuples of the same length.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first tuple of integers.\n        tuple2: The second tuple of integers (divisors).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the results of the element-wise modulo operations.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input tuples have different lengths.\n        ZeroDivisionError: If any element in tuple2 is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        results.append(tuple1[i] % tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(results)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "```python\nclass ListOperationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for list operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\nclass ListLengthMismatchError(ListOperationError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when lists have different lengths for element-wise operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input lists must have the same length.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass DivisionByZeroError(ListOperationError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an attempt to divide by zero occurs during element-wise division.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Division by zero encountered.\", index: int = -1):\n        self.index = index\n        super().__init__(f\"{message} at index {index}.\")\n\ndef div_list(list1: list[float | int], list2: list[float | int]) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Divides two lists element-wise.\n\n    Args:\n        list1: The dividend list.\n        list2: The divisor list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the results of the division.\n\n    Raises:\n        ListLengthMismatchError: If the input lists have different lengths.\n        DivisionByZeroError: If any element in list2 is zero.\n        TypeError: If lists contain non-numeric types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ListLengthMismatchError()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        if not isinstance(list1[i], (int, float)) or not isinstance(list2[i], (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Non-numeric type found at index {i}. Both elements must be int or float.\")\n        if list2[i] == 0:\n            raise DivisionByZeroError(index=i)\n        result.append(float(list1[i]) / list2[i])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise modulo operation on two tuples of the same length.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first tuple (dividend).\n        tuple2: The second tuple (divisor).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the results of the element-wise modulo operations.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If either input is not a tuple.\n        ValueError: If the input tuples have different lengths.\n        ZeroDivisionError: If any element in tuple2 is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if tuple2[i] == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(f\"Modulo by zero at index {i}.\")\n        result.append(tuple1[i] % tuple2[i])\n\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
