{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\nclass BaseListOperationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for all list operation errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass ListLengthMismatchError(BaseListOperationError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when two lists have different lengths for an element-wise operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input lists must have the same length.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass DivisionByZeroError(BaseListOperationError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an attempt is made to divide by zero during an element-wise operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Cannot divide by zero.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef div_list(list_a: List[Union[float, int]], list_b: List[Union[float, int]]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Divides two lists element-wise.\n\n    Args:\n        list_a: The numerator list.\n        list_b: The denominator list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the float results of the element-wise division.\n\n    Raises:\n        ListLengthMismatchError: If the input lists have different lengths.\n        DivisionByZeroError: If any element in list_b is zero.\n        TypeError: If list elements are not numeric (handled by Python's / operator).\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list_a) != len(list_b):\n        raise ListLengthMismatchError(\n            f\"Lists must have the same length. Got {len(list_a)} and {len(list_b)}.\"\n        )\n\n    results: List[float] = []\n    for i in range(len(list_a)):\n        numerator = list_a[i]\n        denominator = list_b[i]\n\n        if denominator == 0:\n            raise DivisionByZeroError(f\"Cannot divide by zero at index {i}.\")\n\n        results.append(float(numerator) / float(denominator))\n\n    return results\n```\n"}
