{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest divisible subset from a list of numbers.\n    A subset is divisible if every pair (a, b) within it satisfies a % b == 0 or b % a == 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    has_zero = False\n    non_zeros = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num == 0:\n            has_zero = True\n        else:\n            non_zeros.append(num)\n\n    # Sort non_zeros to apply dynamic programming.\n    # This allows building subsets where smaller numbers divide larger ones.\n    non_zeros.sort()\n\n    if not non_zeros:\n        return 1 if has_zero else 0\n\n    # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with non_zeros[i].\n    dp = [1] * len(non_zeros)\n    max_subset_size_non_zeros = 1\n\n    for i in range(len(non_zeros)):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if non_zeros[i] % non_zeros[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], 1 + dp[j])\n        max_subset_size_non_zeros = max(max_subset_size_non_zeros, dp[i])\n\n    # If zero is present, the largest subset is either [0] (size 1)\n    # or the largest subset found among non-zero numbers.\n    if has_zero:\n        return max(1, max_subset_size_non_zeros)\n    return max_subset_size_non_zeros\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is divisible.\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming after sorting the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    nums.sort()  # Sort the list to enable dynamic programming efficiently.\n    dp = [1] * n # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with nums[i].\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            a = nums[i]\n            b = nums[j]\n\n            # Check if 'a' and 'b' form a divisible pair, handling zero cases.\n            is_divisible_pair = False\n            if b == 0:\n                is_divisible_pair = (a == 0)\n            elif a == 0:\n                is_divisible_pair = True\n            else:\n                is_divisible_pair = (a % b == 0 or b % a == 0)\n\n            if is_divisible_pair:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], 1 + dp[j])\n\n    return max(dp)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of equal size.\n    It conceptually merges the lists to find the two middle elements in O(N) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2\n    m1 = -1\n    m2 = -1\n\n    # The loop runs 'size + 1' times to find the (size-1)-th and size-th elements\n    # of the conceptually merged sorted list.\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        if i == size: # If list1 is exhausted, take from list2\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size: # If list2 is exhausted, take from list1\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]: # Compare current elements and pick the smaller\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists, list1 and list2, each of size n.\n    It returns the median of the combined 2n elements as a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1.\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2.\n    count = 0\n    m1 = -1  # Stores the n-th smallest element.\n    m2 = -1  # Stores the (n+1)-th smallest element.\n\n    # Iterate through both lists to find the n-th and (n+1)-th elements\n    # in the merged sorted order.\n    while count <= n:\n        if i == n:  # All elements of list1 have been considered.\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:  # All elements of list2 have been considered.\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        count += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/623", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef nth_nums(nums: List[Union[int, float]], n: int) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th power of each number in a list.\n\n    Args:\n        nums: A list of numbers (integers or floats).\n        n: An integer representing the power.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list where each element is the n-th power of the corresponding\n        element in the input list.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If inputs are not of the expected types or values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(nums, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'nums' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} in 'nums' is not a number: {num}\")\n        results.append(num ** n)\n    return results\n```"}
