{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of XOR of all unique pairs in a list of numbers.\n    The `length` parameter is trusted to match `len(numbers)`.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (numbers[i], numbers[j]) where i < j.\n    for i in range(length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            total_xor_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n            \n    return total_xor_sum\n```"}
