{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef _heapify(arr: list[int | float], n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    A helper function to maintain the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\n    It ensures the subtree at 'i' satisfies the max-heap property.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest = i  # Initialize largest as root\n    left = 2 * i + 1  # left child\n    right = 2 * i + 2  # right child\n\n    # See if left child of root exists and is greater than root\n    if left < n and arr[largest] < arr[left]:\n        largest = left\n\n    # See if right child of root exists and is greater than largest so far\n    if right < n and arr[largest] < arr[right]:\n        largest = right\n\n    # Change root, if needed\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]  # swap\n        # Recursively heapify the affected sub-tree.\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\ndef heap_sort(arr: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It builds a max-heap and then repeatedly extracts the maximum element.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Build a maxheap. The last parent will be at index (n // 2 - 1).\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from the heap.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Move current root to end.\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call heapify on the reduced heap.\n    \n    return arr\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef _heapify(data: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maintains the max-heap property in a subtree rooted at index i.\n    n is the size of the heap.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and data[largest] < data[left]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and data[largest] < data[right]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        data[i], data[largest] = data[largest], data[i]\n        _heapify(data, n, largest)\n\ndef _build_max_heap(data: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a max-heap from the given list in-place.\n    It calls _heapify for all non-leaf nodes.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data)\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(data, n, i)\n\ndef heap_sort(data: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new list with elements in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data)\n    temp_list = list(data)\n\n    _build_max_heap(temp_list)\n\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        temp_list[i], temp_list[0] = temp_list[0], temp_list[i]\n        _heapify(temp_list, i, 0)\n\n    return temp_list\n```"}
