{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef wind_chill(velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the wind chill index based on Environment Canada's formula.\n    The result is rounded up to the nearest integer.\n\n    Args:\n        velocity: The wind velocity in kilometers per hour (km/h).\n        temperature: The air temperature in Celsius.\n\n    Returns:\n        The wind chill index as an integer, rounded up.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If wind velocity is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input: Wind velocity cannot be negative.\n    if velocity < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Wind velocity cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Constants for the Environment Canada Wind Chill Index formula.\n    C1 = 13.12\n    C2 = 0.6215\n    C3 = 11.37\n    C4 = 0.3965\n    EXPONENT = 0.16\n\n    # Handle zero velocity as a special case where wind chill equals temperature.\n    if velocity == 0:\n        raw_wind_chill = temperature\n    else:\n        # Calculate V^0.16 term and apply the Environment Canada Wind Chill Index formula.\n        v_exponent = velocity ** EXPONENT\n        raw_wind_chill = (\n            C1\n            + C2 * temperature\n            - C3 * v_exponent\n            + C4 * temperature * v_exponent\n        )\n\n    # Round up the calculated wind chill index to the next highest integer using math.ceil.\n    return math.ceil(raw_wind_chill)\n```"}
