{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "```python\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Multiplies adjacent elements in a tuple of numbers.\n    Returns an empty tuple if the input has fewer than two elements.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a tuple or if any element is not a number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        t_i = input_tuple[i]\n        t_i_plus_1 = input_tuple[i+1]\n\n        if not isinstance(t_i, (int, float)) or not isinstance(t_i_plus_1, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the tuple must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n        result.append(t_i * t_i_plus_1)\n    \n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Union\n\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]) -> Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a tuple of numbers and returns a new tuple where the i-th element\n    is the product of the i-th and (i+1)-th elements of the input tuple.\n\n    Args:\n        input_tuple: A tuple of integers or floats.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple with the products of adjacent elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If input_tuple is not a tuple or contains non-numeric elements.\n        ValueError: If input_tuple has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuple must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        t_i = input_tuple[i]\n        t_i_plus_1 = input_tuple[i+1]\n\n        if not isinstance(t_i, (int, float)) or not isinstance(t_i_plus_1, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the tuple must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n        result.append(t_i * t_i_plus_1)\n\n    return tuple(result)\n"}
