{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "import math\n\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r: float, h: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a cone given radius r and height h.\n\n    Args:\n        r: The radius of the cone's base. Must be non-negative.\n        h: The perpendicular height of the cone. Must be non-negative.\n\n    Returns:\n        The lateral surface area of the cone.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If radius or height are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if r < 0 or h < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius and height must be non-negative.\")\n\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(r**2 + h**2)\n    lateral_surface_area = math.pi * r * slant_height\n    return lateral_surface_area"}
