{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index, or -1 if not found or the array is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(arr, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of a target number in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index if found, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    first_occurrence_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            first_occurrence_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Continue searching in the left half for an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    \n    return first_occurrence_index\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(numbers: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of products of all possible sublists from a given list of numbers.\n    The function iterates through all contiguous sublists and sums their element products.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    # Iterate through all possible start indices\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Iterate through all possible end indices\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            current_product = 1\n            # Calculate product for the sublist from i to j\n            for k in range(i, j + 1):\n                current_product *= numbers[k]\n            total_sum += current_product\n    \n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of products of all possible sublists from the given list of integers.\n    This function adheres to the core logic specified for advanced list analysis.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_product = 1\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            current_product *= numbers[j]\n            total_sum += current_product\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Toggles all bits of the number except its most significant bit (MSB) and least significant bit (LSB).\n    Returns an integer with its middle bits toggled.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    binary_str = bin(number)[2:]\n\n    if len(binary_str) <= 2:\n        return number\n\n    msb = binary_str[0]\n    lsb = binary_str[-1]\n    middle_bits = binary_str[1:-1]\n\n    toggled_middle_bits = ''.join(['1' if bit == '0' else '0' for bit in middle_bits])\n\n    result_binary_str = msb + toggled_middle_bits + lsb\n    return int(result_binary_str, 2)\n```"}
