{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the index k of the smallest triangular number that has exactly n digits.\n    The input n is assumed to be a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_value = 10**(n - 1)\n\n    # Approximate k using k * (k + 1) / 2 >= min_value => k^2 approx 2 * min_value\n    k = int(math.sqrt(2 * min_value))\n\n    # Adjust k if the approximation was too low\n    while k * (k + 1) // 2 < min_value:\n        k += 1\n    \n    return k\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    The iteration starts from k=1 and continues until T_k meets the digit requirement.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the lower bound for an n-digit number.\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1)\n\n    # Start checking from k=1 for triangular numbers.\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        # Calculate the k-th triangular number.\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        \n        # If the current triangular number has at least n digits, it's our target.\n        if triangular_number >= lower_bound:\n            return k\n        k += 1\n```"}
