{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds self-dividing numbers within a given range.\n    A number is self-dividing if every digit (excluding zero) divides it evenly.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _get_digits(num: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a number.\"\"\"\n        return [int(d) for d in str(num)]\n\n    def _is_self_dividing(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single number is self-dividing.\"\"\"\n        digits = _get_digits(num)\n\n        if 0 in digits:\n            return False\n\n        for digit in digits:\n            if num % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_self_dividing(num):\n            result.append(num)\n            \n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds numbers in a range that are divisible by each of their non-zero digits. Numbers containing '0' are excluded.\"\"\"\n    \n    self_divisible_numbers = []\n    \n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        str_num = str(number)\n        is_current_num_self_divisible = True\n        \n        for char_digit in str_num:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            \n            # Exclude numbers containing '0' as per Business Rule 1.\n            if digit == 0:\n                is_current_num_self_divisible = False\n                break\n            \n            # Check if the number is divisible by the current digit.\n            if number % digit != 0:\n                is_current_num_self_divisible = False\n                break\n        \n        if is_current_num_self_divisible:\n            self_divisible_numbers.append(number)\n            \n    return self_divisible_numbers\n```"}
