{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts a space before each uppercase letter that is not the first character of the string,\n    provided it is not already preceded by a space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n    # Use regex to insert a space before any uppercase letter that meets the conditions.\n    # The lookbehind `(?<!^)` ensures we don't add a space at the start.\n    # The lookbehind `(?<! )` ensures we don't add a space if one already exists.\n    # `\\1` re-inserts the matched uppercase letter after the new space.\n    return re.sub(r'(?<!^)(?<! )([A-Z])', r' \\1', input_string)\n```"}
