{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    Assumes `arr` is a list of comparable elements.\"\"\"\n\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # An empty or single-element array is always a valid min-heap.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate from the last parent node down to the root.\n    # The last parent node's index is (n // 2) - 1.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # If left child exists and is smaller than parent, it's not a min-heap.\n        if left_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        # If right child exists and is smaller than parent, it's not a min-heap.\n        if right_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    Returns True if it's a min-heap, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only up to the last parent node\n    # The last parent node is at index (n // 2) - 1\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number iteratively.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer based on critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Corresponds to J(0) and J(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_jacobsthal = b + 2 * a\n        a, b = b, next_jacobsthal\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number.\n    J(0)=0, J(1)=1, and J(n) = J(n-1) + 2*J(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize with J(0) and J(1)\n    # a stores J(k-2), b stores J(k-1)\n    a, b = 0, 1 \n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Calculate J(k) using J(k-1) and J(k-2)\n        a, b = b, b + 2 * a\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\ndef min_k(records, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds k records with the smallest values from a list of (name, value) tuples.\n    Returns an empty list if k is non-positive or the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0 or not records:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the list of tuples based on the 'value' (second element) in ascending order.\n    # Slicing handles cases where k is greater than the list's length.\n    sorted_records = sorted(records, key=lambda x: x[1])\n    return sorted_records[:k]\n```"}
