{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts unique pairs of strings where one is the reverse of the other.\n    Each string can participate in at most one pair, and palindromes don't pair with themselves.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    encountered_strings = set()\n\n    for s in string_list:\n        s_reverse = s[::-1]\n        # Check if the reverse exists and is not the same string (to handle palindromes)\n        if s_reverse in encountered_strings and s != s_reverse:\n            count += 1\n            encountered_strings.remove(s_reverse)\n        else:\n            encountered_strings.add(s)\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique reverse string pairs in the given list.\n    A pair (s1, s2) is counted if s1 is the reverse of s2, s1 != s2, and the pair is unique.\n    \"\"\"\n    candidates = set(string_list)\n    reverse_pairs_count = 0\n    processed_pairs = set()\n\n    for s in candidates:\n        reversed_s = s[::-1]\n\n        if s != reversed_s and reversed_s in candidates:\n            pair = tuple(sorted((s, reversed_s)))\n            if pair not in processed_pairs:\n                reverse_pairs_count += 1\n                processed_pairs.add(pair)\n    \n    return reverse_pairs_count\n```"}
