{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr: tuple[int | float, ...], n: int) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the given array.\n    This function assumes the input array has at least two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_arr = sorted(list(arr))\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted array to find the minimum difference between adjacent elements.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = abs(sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    return min_diff\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr, N):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in a given array.\n    Assumes the input array contains at least two numerical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_arr = sorted(list(arr))\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        diff = sorted_arr[i] - sorted_arr[i-1]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    return min_diff\n```"}
