{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    def _is_power_of_two(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer is a power of two.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 0:  # Polite numbers are positive integers.\n            return False\n        return (num & (num - 1)) == 0\n\n    polite_count = 0\n    current_num = 1\n    while True:\n        if not _is_power_of_two(current_num):\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return current_num\n        current_num += 1\n```\n"}
