{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef get_pairs_count(list_of_numbers: List[Union[int, float]], sum: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs in a list that sum to a target value.\n    This function efficiently finds all such pairs using a frequency map.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    # Build frequency map\n    freq_map = {}\n    for x in list_of_numbers:\n        freq_map[x] = freq_map.get(x, 0) + 1\n    \n    pair_count = 0\n\n    for num in list_of_numbers:\n        # Decrement count of current number to avoid self-pairing with the same instance.\n        # This also correctly handles duplicate numbers when num is equal to its complement.\n        if freq_map[num] > 0:\n            freq_map[num] -= 1\n        else:\n            # If the count is 0, this specific instance of 'num' has already been used in a pair.\n            continue\n\n        complement = sum - num\n\n        # If complement exists in the map and its count is greater than 0, add its count to total.\n        if complement in freq_map and freq_map[complement] > 0:\n            pair_count += freq_map[complement]\n\n    return pair_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], target_sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs in a list that sum to a target value, treating duplicates by index.\n    Achieves O(N) average time complexity using a hash map for frequency counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    freq_map = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        freq_map[num] = freq_map.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    pair_count = 0\n\n    # Iterate over a copy of keys to safely modify the dictionary during iteration\n    for num in list(freq_map.keys()):\n        if freq_map.get(num, 0) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        complement = target_sum - num\n\n        if complement == num:\n            # If the complement is the same number, count combinations of this number with itself\n            frequency = freq_map[num]\n            pair_count += frequency * (frequency - 1) // 2\n            freq_map[num] = 0\n        elif complement in freq_map and freq_map[complement] > 0:\n            # If complement is different and exists, multiply their frequencies\n            pair_count += freq_map[num] * freq_map[complement]\n            freq_map[num] = 0\n            freq_map[complement] = 0\n\n    return pair_count\n```"}
