{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given expression string has balanced brackets.\n    Ignores non-bracket characters and uses a stack-based approach.\"\"\"\n\n    # Define bracket constants directly within the function scope.\n    OPENING_BRACKETS = \"([{\"\n    CLOSING_BRACKETS = \")]}\"\n    BRACKET_MAP = {\n        \")\": \"(\",\n        \"]\": \"[\",\n        \"}\": \"{\",\n    }\n\n    stack = []\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_BRACKETS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_BRACKETS:\n            # If stack is empty or the top element doesn't match the closing bracket, it's unbalanced.\n            if not stack or stack[-1] != BRACKET_MAP[char]:\n                return False\n            stack.pop()\n    \n    # The expression is balanced if the stack is empty at the end.\n    return not stack\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression has balanced brackets.\n    It ignores non-bracket characters and validates bracket order.\n    \"\"\"\n    OPENING_BRACKETS = {'(', '[', '{'}\n    CLOSING_BRACKETS = {')', ']', '}'}\n    BRACKET_MAP = {\n        ')': '(',\n        ']': '[',\n        '}': '{'\n    }\n\n    stack = []\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_BRACKETS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_BRACKETS:\n            if not stack:\n                return False  # Closing bracket with no corresponding opener.\n            \n            last_open = stack.pop()\n            if BRACKET_MAP[char] != last_open:\n                return False  # Mismatched opening and closing bracket types.\n    \n    return not stack # Returns True if all opening brackets were correctly closed.\n```"}
