{"task_id": "Mbpp/785", "solution": "class InvalidTupleStringError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception indicating a string could not be parsed into an integer tuple.\n    Inherits from ValueError for semantic consistency with Python\\'s built-in exceptions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef tuple_str_int(tuple_str: str) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Converts a string representation of an integer tuple into an actual integer tuple.\n    Raises InvalidTupleStringError for malformed inputs or non-integer elements.\"\"\"\n\n    if not (tuple_str.startswith('(') and tuple_str.endswith(')')):\n        raise InvalidTupleStringError(\"Input string must start with '(' and end with ')'.\")\n\n    if tuple_str == \"()\":\n        return ()\n\n    content = tuple_str[1:-1]\n    elements_str = content.split(',')\n\n    result = []\n    for element_str in elements_str:\n        stripped_element = element_str.strip()\n\n        try:\n            integer_value = int(stripped_element)\n            result.append(integer_value)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise InvalidTupleStringError(f\"Element '{element_str}' is not a valid integer. Details: {e}\")\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef right_insertion(sorted_list: List[Any], value: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    The returned index ensures the list remains sorted, inserting after equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
