{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last occurrence of a target element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the 0-based index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if not found or array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Found target, now try to find further right.\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
