{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are positive integers (>= 1).\n\n    Args:\n        l: The lower bound of the range.\n        r: The upper bound of the range.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of all odd natural numbers in the specified range.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If l or r are not integers, or if l > r.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, int) or not isinstance(r, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both l and r must be integers.\")\n    if l > r:\n        raise ValueError(\"Lower bound (l) cannot be greater than upper bound (r).\")\n\n    # Ensure we only consider natural numbers (positive integers >= 1)\n    # The effective lower bound for natural numbers is at least 1.\n    effective_l = max(1, l)\n\n    # If the effective range for natural numbers is empty, return 0.\n    if effective_l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Helper function to calculate the sum of odd positive integers up to n\n    def _sum_positive_odd_up_to(n: int) -> int:\n        if n < 1:\n            return 0\n        # The sum of the first k odd positive numbers is k^2.\n        # The count of odd numbers up to n is (n + 1) // 2.\n        k = (n + 1) // 2\n        return k * k\n\n    # Calculate the sum of odd natural numbers up to r\n    sum_up_to_r = _sum_positive_odd_up_to(r)\n\n    # Calculate the sum of odd natural numbers up to (effective_l - 1)\n    sum_up_to_effective_l_minus_1 = _sum_positive_odd_up_to(effective_l - 1)\n\n    return sum_up_to_r - sum_up_to_effective_l_minus_1\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are positive integers (1, 2, 3, ...).\n    \"\"\"\n    if l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in range(l, r + 1):\n        if num >= 1 and num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
