{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit unsigned integer to the left by 'd' positions.\n    The rotation wraps around and ensures the result is a 32-bit unsigned integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_WIDTH = 32\n    MAX_VALUE = (1 << BIT_WIDTH) - 1\n\n    # Ensure d is effectively within 0 to BIT_WIDTH-1 for rotation logic.\n    d = d % BIT_WIDTH\n\n    # Perform left rotation. Bits shifted off the left re-enter on the right.\n    return ((number << d) | (number >> (BIT_WIDTH - d))) & MAX_VALUE\n```"}
