{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "```python\ndef is_perfect_square(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is a perfect square.\"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Binary search to find the integer square root.\n    low = 1\n    high = number\n    root_candidate = 0\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        square = mid * mid\n\n        if square == number:\n            return True\n        elif square < number:\n            root_candidate = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n            \n    return root_candidate * root_candidate == number\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "```python\ndef is_perfect_square(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer is a perfect square.\n    Handles negative numbers and zero as specified by the requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if n < 0:\n        return False\n    if n == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Define an inline helper for integer square root using binary search.\n    # This avoids calling external utilities like math.isqrt.\n    def _isqrt_inline(x: int) -> int:\n        if x == 1:\n            return 1\n\n        low, high = 1, x // 2\n        ans = 1 # Stores floor(sqrt(x)) found so far\n\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if mid * mid == x:\n                return mid\n            elif mid * mid < x:\n                ans = mid # mid is a possible candidate for floor(sqrt(x))\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return ans\n\n    sqrt_n = _isqrt_inline(n)\n    return sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/804", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef is_product_even(numbers: list[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the product of numbers in a list is an even integer.\n    The product of an empty list is 1 (odd).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return False\n\n    product: float = 1.0\n    for num in numbers:\n        product *= num\n\n    # Check if the product is an integer and then if it's even.\n    if product.is_integer():\n        return int(product) % 2 == 0\n    else:\n        return False\n```"}
