{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "```python\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two tuples element-wise, checking if every element in tuple2 is strictly smaller than tuple1.\n    Returns False if tuple lengths differ or if any corresponding element fails the strict less than condition.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        return False\n    \n    for e1, e2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if not (e2 < e1):\n            return False\n            \n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "```python\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its\n    corresponding element in the first tuple. Returns True if all elements in\n    tuple2 are smaller, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if not (tuple2[i] < tuple1[i]):\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
